 "assumptions": [
  "Protonation states and partial charges come from AMBER ff14SB (+ OL15 DNA, OL3 RNA). ASP and GLU are anionic. LYS and ARG are cationic. CYS and TYR are neutral. HIS is HIE by default. A tautomer name in the file (HID/HIE/HIP, HSD/HSE/HSP) or its hydrogens override this default. Changes for single residues override everything.",
  "Cys pairs with S–S < 2.5 Å are disulfides (CYX). Chain termini are charged (NH₃⁺, COO⁻). Residues next to a chain break are treated as internal.",
  "Fragment 1 of the QM region is the whole halogenated ligand. Fragment 2 holds the whole acceptor residues. Residues within 5 Å of the halogen are added.",
  "Missing hydrogens follow the force-field template of each residue (number of H per atom) with VSEPR geometry. Cut bonds get H caps (fixed X–H length).",
  "Ligands: one heavy-atom structure fixes the hydrogens and the charge. Every sp² carbon gets one double bond. The keto form is preferred. An sp² ring N without a double bond carries one H. P keeps one P=O bond. S keeps up to two S=O bonds. At pH 7, COOH, phosphate, phosphonate, sulfonate and sulfate groups lose their O–H hydrogen. Amines stay neutral. Hydrogens of the file stay only with a matching number. The PDB formula (FORMUL) checks the count.",
  "Fragment charges: residue formal charges come from the force-field template. The ligand charge comes from a loaded MOL2 file or from the ligand structure above. Every value can be overridden.",
  "The QM cluster sits in an implicit dielectric ε = 4 (CPCM/PCM). The dielectric represents the protein."
 ],
